{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles","id":1109015,"title":"Mirrors in Chronicles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-28T16:22:39-07:00","id":1109015,"title":"Mirrors in Chronicles","content":"Something occurred to me recently. Mirrors was a very interesting book for pre-Chronicles nWoD. I think some of the concepts there made it to Chronicles, but I'm not sure. I know that the concept of Conviction and &quot;skill tricks&quot; which I remember there didn't, though. Has anyone tried to use those rules with Chronicles-era books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T18:36:07-07:00","id":1109069,"title":"","content":"I know that some of the Skill Tricks are redundant or not very impressive when compared to 2ED stuff. They would need changes in order to keep up. Conviction itself is nice, but is likewise underwhelming when compared to all the power boosts that the splats have gotten so far in 2ED.<br /> <br /> For example: the Flashing Blades Skill Trick for Weaponry is covered in 2ED by Defensive Combat (Weaponry), the second Maneuver of the Heavy Weapons Style and the fourth Maneuver of the Light Weapons Style. For a 2ED version, Flashing Blades could instead give 8 Again to Dodging when you have your weapon drawn, increase the weapon's Damage Bonus by one, and increase your Defense by [your Weaponry/2 round up]. That does not make the aforementioned 2ED Merits obsolete, but also gives a new function to the Skill Trick which works well with Light Weapons, Heavy Weapons and Armed Defense.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Could we use this thread for sharing ideas on how to update Mirrors to 2ED?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-28-2017, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T22:12:52-07:00","id":1109114,"title":"","content":"Infinite Macabre's Spaceship system needs an Overhaul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T04:42:25-07:00","id":1109181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1109069#post1109069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that some of the Skill Tricks are redundant or not very impressive when compared to 2ED stuff. They would need changes in order to keep up. Conviction itself is nice, but is likewise underwhelming when compared to all the power boosts that the splats have gotten so far in 2ED.<br /> <br /> For example: the Flashing Blades Skill Trick for Weaponry is covered in 2ED by Defensive Combat (Weaponry), the second Maneuver of the Heavy Weapons Style and the fourth Maneuver of the Light Weapons Style. For a 2ED version, Flashing Blades could instead give 8 Again to Dodging when you have your weapon drawn, increase the weapon's Damage Bonus by one, and increase your Defense by [your Weaponry/2 round up]. That does not make the aforementioned 2ED Merits obsolete, but also gives a new function to the Skill Trick which works well with Light Weapons, Heavy Weapons and Armed Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. The baseline &quot;power level&quot; (for lack of a better term) of Chronicles has risen, on average, so special mechanics for larger-than-life mundane skills should have to be beefier, as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Could we use this thread for sharing ideas on how to update Mirrors to 2ED? </div> </div> </div>Doing that is one of the reasons I made it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T15:57:48-07:00","id":1109450,"title":"","content":"*spins up arm sore from International Travel.* Well, first off, the main point of Mirrors is that its a tool kit, most of its material is as a result configurable or addable, such as revision initiative, trading Willpower to affect World Building (I love this one so much), and so on. that stuff is cheap and simple enough any revising is going to be simplistic and not really noteworthy and really acts as Addons or replacements to existing material.<br /> <br /> Less easy is the &quot;Mirrors&quot; setting material. Woundgate, Bleeding Edge, and Infinite Macabre are all fascinating, but their mechanics often aren't often well defined, some exceptions exist, but in general, these things have issues due to being too sparse. They largely have good settings, but lack mechanics<br /> <br /> Just going off of memory:<br /> Woundgate needs more &quot;stuff&quot; plainly, and a good prefab list of Cities to draw from. I guess it's made for customization and to save costs.<br /> <br /> Bleeding Edge just doesn't have enough Cyberware, I am so sorry and I understand that this was done to save costs, but having to reference other supernatural powers is a tad lazy and requires having other books to make use of it. It's especially bad because the cost of these powers was tied towards the cost of getting that power... ignoring that for many supernaturals the cost involves more than just paying Exp. I would also drop Willpower as a cost if you're going to charge Cyberware any resource cost and have universal batteries or something. I do like the Alienation effect though, that was pretty neat.<br /> <br /> Infinite Macabre simply needs more detail with ships and a dedicated Ship to Ship combat system. I still feel upset fighters and battleships can get the same value on weapons and health was kinda shallow in a way since a fighter was 20 HP, but a battlestation was only 100. I'd prefer if there was different types of gear, largely to make more variety in spaceship combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 06-29-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-29T16:35:21-07:00","id":1109471,"title":"","content":"<b>Re:Mirrors </b><br /> <br /> Mirrors is one of my favorite books in the nWoD/CofD line(but I am a sucker for game supplements that give you ways to tinker with base mechanics of the game). But in retrospect it is very much a book that was put out when the overall future of the gameline was really murky and they were trying to get some material out in case the line was canceled entirely. Many of the ideas presented could have easily been standalone books with development. Its pretty telling that many of the proposed mechanics in Mirrors (and other books like Danse Macabre) ended up in 2nd Edition.<br /> That being said, I am going to go over my design notes and see if I can contribute some ideas that can give some of the presented ideas a bit more polish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T08:34:32-07:00","id":1138328,"title":"","content":"Going over the Dark Hero Template, two Masteries seemed especially inappropriate for 2ED: Powerful Success and Rapidity. Here are my proposed fixes:<br /> <br /> <b>Powerful Success:</b> Reduce the number of Successes required for an Exceptional Success by (Arete). Each dot of Arete from 6 upward gives an automatic Success. For rolls where more Successes are their own reward, such as combat, add (Arete/2 round up) as bonus Successes, or (Arete) with 1 Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Rapidity x 1:</b> If your Skill rating is equal or greater than that of an opponent, you may attempt to interrupt their roll, as long as they are within ([Arete + 1] x Speed) yards. You do not have to use the same Skill as the one that is being interrupted, but the ST decides which combinations are appropriate. Every Success you gain reduces their Successes by one. Should the opponent's Skill rating exceed yours, you may make up for the difference by spending 1 Willpower point. You may interrupt rolls a number of times per scene equal to Arete. Should the opponent have a power that would counter this, roll for a Clash Of Wills against the Dark Hero's Arete + Skill. If there is no opponent immediately present, divide the Target Number of Successes for Extended Actions by (Arete/2 round up) + 1 and divide the time taken per each roll by (Arete + 1), round down.<br /> <br /> <b>Rapidity x 2:</b> Your Skill gains the Advanced Action benefit. If you reduce your opponent's Successes to zero, each Success you gain after that may be spent on your own counter-action. You may spend 1 Willpower point to immediately reduce his Successes to zero and then apply all of your Successes as a counter-action (this cannot be done if the opponent's Skill rating exceeds yours). If no opponent is immediately present, you may spend 1 Willpower point to make a number of rolls equal to Arete for Extended Actions take one turn. This may be used to complete one Extended Action much faster, or be distributed among multiple Extended Actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-07-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T10:34:20-07:00","id":1138351,"title":"","content":"I don't really see what's wrong with Powerful Successes as-written.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T21:49:29-07:00","id":1138496,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a> Do you still plan on posting your design notes in this thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T16:53:18-07:00","id":1138748,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Mirrors Updates</b><br /> <br /> I haven't had the chance to look at this project in quite some time. I was putting together something for the Cybernetics in Bleeding Edge. I was thinking about treating Cybernetics in a similar way to how Supernatural Merits are currently, but got stuck on finding the right balance point between writing up specific augmentations that do specific things (like in Shadowrun), or keeping the merits effect-based and letting the player decide what it looks like and how it functions. I was also considering a &quot;cyber-psychosis&quot; effect - its a cyberpunk staple that the more chrome you get the more mentally imbalanced you become, which makes sense through a CofD lense. I will review what I have and see if I can hammer it into something workable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T06:41:22-07:00","id":1138874,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Augmentations </b><br /> <br /> I did a quick revision of my notes - these are fairly bare-bones mechanics that are light on examples and I'm still not certain what would be the best approach for blatantly inhuman capabilities. but have a look and lets see how we can fine tune these ideas. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Augmentation</b></span><br /> <br /> Augmentations represent artificial modifications to a characters body that greatly enhance its capabilities, in certain cases to a superhuman degree. These augmentations typically represent cybernetic or genetic modification, but could be used to represent mystic alterations as well. The merits represent basic capabilities, how these manifest or are described is up to the storyteller and players to decide.<br /> The over-all number of dots in Augmentation merits a character can have is limited to (10 + the lower of Resolve or Stamina). In addition, if the total number in dots in Augmentation ever exceed the characters (Resolve + Composure), they suffer a -1 penalty to Breaking Point rolls. There is only so much strain the body and mind can withstand.<br /> <br /> Most supernatural creatures cannot take augmentation \u2013 their physiological and metaphysical natures often confound the complicated and delicate technologies needed to successfully apply augmentations. Supernatural beings that are still human (as least physiologically speaking) may be able to use Augmentations (at Storyteller\u2019s discretion)<br /> <br /> <b>Enhancement </b><b>(\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Enhancements improve an individual\u2019s physical or neurological makeup. When this merit is selected, choose a physical or mental attribute. The character may spend a point of Willpower to gain a +1 increase to the chosen attribute, which effects derived values and may exceed the character dot limit in that attribute. This bonus lasts until the end of the scene. This merit may be selected multiple times, each selection applying to a different attribute. The 5 dot version increases the bonus to +2.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>A dramatic failure while using the Enhancement causes it to malfunction. For the remainder of the scene, the Enhancement cannot be re-activated and rolls using the associated attribute suffer a -1 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Implant (\u2022+; </b>Special<b>)</b><br /> An Implant is an alteration that integrates an item or device into your physiology. This device can be nearly any weapon or technological piece of equipment. This merit may be taken multiple times, each time representing a different implant. The benefits and associated merit costs are as follow;<br /> <b>Armor (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Implanted Armor gives a bonus the characters armor rating. All of these are considered to grant coverage of the legs, arms, and torso. The character gains armor 1/3 or 2/0 at two dots. The four dot version grants armor 2/4, but suffers a -1 penalty to defense.<br /> <b>Equipment (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022): </b>Implanted Equipment can be nearly any item that grants an equipment bonus or special feature. Such a device must be size 2 or less, and its cost in merit dots is equal to the higher of its Availability or Equipment Bonus.<br /> <b>Merit: </b>An implant can replicate the effects of a physical or mental merit at equivalent cost. It may also replicate the effects of the Striking Looks social merit. At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, an implant may be able to replicate supernatural merits as well.<br /> <b>Weapons (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022): </b>Weapon Implants are typically housed in characters limbs, but more exotic locations are possible. At one dots, the weapon may be a size 0 or 1 weapon with availability 2 or less. These devices are small and retractable, giving a +2 bonus to dice rolls when concealing the weapon. The two dot version allows size 2 weapons with availability 3 or less and reduces the concealment bonus to +1. The 3 dot version allows size 3 weapons with availability 3 or less; even with advanced miniaturization, such a device typically replaces the entire limb, is not concealable, and often impedes the use of that limb for actions other than using the weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Plugin </b><b>(\u2022to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A Plugin is an alteration that enhances the characters performance at a certain task. These often represent implants and modifications that greatly enhance capability within a somewhat narrow scope. When this merit is selected, choose an Attribute + Skill pair (such as Intelligence +Computers or Dexterity + Firearms) or an Attribute+ Attribute pair (such as Wits+ Composure) The character may spend a point of Willpower to gain an equipment bonus to the chosen pair equal to the dots in this merit until the end of the scene.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>A dramatic failure while using the Plugin causes the enhancement to malfunction. For the remainder of the scene, the Plugin cannot be re-activated and rolls using the associated attribute + skill pair suffer a -1 penalty.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T08:54:33-07:00","id":1138902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138748#post1138748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Mirrors Updates</b><br /> <br /> I haven't had the chance to look at this project in quite some time. I was putting together something for the Cybernetics in Bleeding Edge. I was thinking about treating Cybernetics in a similar way to how Supernatural Merits are currently, but got stuck on finding the right balance point between writing up specific augmentations that do specific things (like in Shadowrun), or keeping the merits effect-based and letting the player decide what it looks like and how it functions. I was also considering a &quot;cyber-psychosis&quot; effect - its a cyberpunk staple that the more chrome you get the more mentally imbalanced you become, which makes sense through a CofD lense. I will review what I have and see if I can hammer it into something workable.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Cyber-Psychosis, how about each augment (or dot) above a certain threshold (Stamina, Resolve, both?) penalizes Integrity. Either Breaking Point rolls, current amount, max amount, whatever. The most Chromed up are the most unstable, least strong with Abjurations, etc.<br /> <br /> And it can even tie into Shadowrun Cyberzombies - enough Parts can drive one into Soul Loss.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-09-2017, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T10:26:59-07:00","id":1138929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138902#post1138902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For Cyber-Psychosis, how about each augment (or dot) above a certain threshold (Stamina, Resolve, both?) penalizes Integrity. Either Breaking Point rolls, current amount, max amount, whatever. The most Chromed up are the most unstable, least strong with Abjurations, etc.<br /> <br /> And it can even tie into Shadowrun Cyberzombies - enough Parts can drive one into Soul Loss.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ninja'd</div> </div> </div> </div>Can we... not on the cyber-psychosis? Pretty please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T10:59:48-07:00","id":1138940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138929#post1138929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can we... not on the cyber-psychosis? Pretty please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Easy enough to make optional/exclude it. <br /> <br /> It exists solely to serve as mechanical balance on why everyone wouldn't get cyber'd up if they had a choice.<br /> <br /> Baked-in Downsides or blanket scaling vulnerabilities (like electricity vulnerabilities, or something), would achieve similar goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T11:23:48-07:00","id":1138948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138940#post1138940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Easy enough to make optional/exclude it.<br /> <br /> It exists solely to serve as mechanical balance on why everyone wouldn't get cyber'd up if they had a choice.<br /> <br /> Baked-in Downsides or blanket scaling vulnerabilities (like electricity vulnerabilities, or something), would achieve similar goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cyber-psychosis is pretty offensive, though. Let me ask you a question: am I less human because I need prosthetics to fix my hearing? Does that make me less emotionally stable? If I lose a leg and need a replacement, will I be less <i>myself</i>?<br /> <br /> Bring up infections and rejections and all the &quot;fun&quot; stuff that prosthetics and implants cause. Just don't bring ableist garbage into it.<br /> <br /> Danke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T11:37:29-07:00","id":1138950,"title":"","content":"It works for stuff like <i>intelligence </i>augmentations. Am I less myself if a machine is doing some of my thinking for me? Yeah. Probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T12:28:06-07:00","id":1138961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138948#post1138948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cyber-psychosis is pretty offensive, though. Let me ask you a question: am I less human because I need prosthetics to fix my hearing? Does that make me less emotionally stable? If I lose a leg and need a replacement, will I be less <i>myself</i>?<br /> <br /> Bring up infections and rejections and all the &quot;fun&quot; stuff that prosthetics and implants cause. Just don't bring ableist garbage into it.<br /> <br /> Danke.</div> </div> </div> </div>[Joking]Well, if you lose a leg, you are technically 15% or so less yourself, by body mass.[/Joking]<br /> <br /> I think it has been justified as being less spiritually/meta-physically &quot;pure&quot;. Like you are &quot;cheating&quot; or something. It *is* pretty BS, and has some unfortunate implications. And arbitrarily draws a line regarding which tools are &quot;too far&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-09-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T12:32:17-07:00","id":1138963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138950#post1138950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It works for stuff like <i>intelligence </i>augmentations. Am I less myself if a machine is doing some of my thinking for me? Yeah. Probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of Course Not. (Start philosophical_inhibitor.exe)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T12:41:27-07:00","id":1138965,"title":"","content":"A better drawback for physical augmentations might be stuff like phantom limbs and crap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T18:24:27-07:00","id":1139065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138874#post1138874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Augmentations </b><br /> <br /> I did a quick revision of my notes - these are fairly bare-bones mechanics that are light on examples and I'm still not certain what would be the best approach for blatantly inhuman capabilities. but have a look and lets see how we can fine tune these ideas. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Augmentation</b></span><br /> <br /> Augmentations represent artificial modifications to a characters body that greatly enhance its capabilities, in certain cases to a superhuman degree. These augmentations typically represent cybernetic or genetic modification, but could be used to represent mystic alterations as well. The merits represent basic capabilities, how these manifest or are described is up to the storyteller and players to decide.<br /> The over-all number of dots in Augmentation merits a character can have is limited to (10 + the lower of Resolve or Stamina). In addition, if the total number in dots in Augmentation ever exceed the characters (Resolve + Composure), they suffer a -1 penalty to Breaking Point rolls. There is only so much strain the body and mind can withstand.<br /> <br /> Most supernatural creatures cannot take augmentation \u2013 their physiological and metaphysical natures often confound the complicated and delicate technologies needed to successfully apply augmentations. Supernatural beings that are still human (as least physiologically speaking) may be able to use Augmentations (at Storyteller\u2019s discretion)<br /> <br /> <b>Enhancement </b><b>(\u2022\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Enhancements improve an individual\u2019s physical or neurological makeup. When this merit is selected, choose a physical or mental attribute. The character may spend a point of Willpower to gain a +1 increase to the chosen attribute, which effects derived values and may exceed the character dot limit in that attribute. This bonus lasts until the end of the scene. This merit may be selected multiple times, each selection applying to a different attribute. The 5 dot version increases the bonus to +2.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>A dramatic failure while using the Enhancement causes it to malfunction. For the remainder of the scene, the Enhancement cannot be re-activated and rolls using the associated attribute suffer a -1 penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Implant (\u2022+; </b>Special<b>)</b><br /> An Implant is an alteration that integrates an item or device into your physiology. This device can be nearly any weapon or technological piece of equipment. This merit may be taken multiple times, each time representing a different implant. The benefits and associated merit costs are as follow;<br /> <b>Armor (\u2022\u2022 or \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022): </b>Implanted Armor gives a bonus the characters armor rating. All of these are considered to grant coverage of the legs, arms, and torso. The character gains armor 1/3 or 2/0 at two dots. The four dot version grants armor 2/4, but suffers a -1 penalty to defense.<br /> <b>Equipment (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022): </b>Implanted Equipment can be nearly any item that grants an equipment bonus or special feature. Such a device must be size 2 or less, and its cost in merit dots is equal to the higher of its Availability or Equipment Bonus.<br /> <b>Merit: </b>An implant can replicate the effects of a physical or mental merit at equivalent cost. It may also replicate the effects of the Striking Looks social merit. At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, an implant may be able to replicate supernatural merits as well.<br /> <b>Weapons (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022): </b>Weapon Implants are typically housed in characters limbs, but more exotic locations are possible. At one dots, the weapon may be a size 0 or 1 weapon with availability 2 or less. These devices are small and retractable, giving a +2 bonus to dice rolls when concealing the weapon. The two dot version allows size 2 weapons with availability 3 or less and reduces the concealment bonus to +1. The 3 dot version allows size 3 weapons with availability 3 or less; even with advanced miniaturization, such a device typically replaces the entire limb, is not concealable, and often impedes the use of that limb for actions other than using the weapon.<br /> <br /> <b>Plugin </b><b>(\u2022to \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> A Plugin is an alteration that enhances the characters performance at a certain task. These often represent implants and modifications that greatly enhance capability within a somewhat narrow scope. When this merit is selected, choose an Attribute + Skill pair (such as Intelligence +Computers or Dexterity + Firearms) or an Attribute+ Attribute pair (such as Wits+ Composure) The character may spend a point of Willpower to gain an equipment bonus to the chosen pair equal to the dots in this merit until the end of the scene.<br /> <i>Drawback: </i>A dramatic failure while using the Plugin causes the enhancement to malfunction. For the remainder of the scene, the Plugin cannot be re-activated and rolls using the associated attribute + skill pair suffer a -1 penalty.</span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Excelent work as always. <br /> <br /> <br /> I actually tried several times to adapt the entire Augmentations lisy grom Shadowrun and a few other places.<br /> <br /> <br /> In general, i found that lots of augments are redundant or were covered by other items if ported into the CoD ruleset.... you dont need to differentiate between cultured muscles and cyber muscles. Additionally, stuff like Cyberarms having specific stats aligned with them didnt need to be, nor woupd be helpful in WoD.....<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It does give me an idea though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T18:28:23-07:00","id":1139067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138965#post1138965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A better drawback for physical augmentations might be stuff like phantom limbs and crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the type of augmentations, you could either become more vulnerable to enemies trying to hack your body parts or disable them with specific toxins. You might also need to spend a certain amount of Resources every so often to get some repairs, or suffer Tilts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T20:16:31-07:00","id":1139083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1109015-mirrors-in-chronicles?p=1138965#post1138965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A better drawback for physical augmentations might be stuff like phantom limbs and crap.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> One way you could handle it:<br /> <br /> Getting a new augmentation is a Breaking Point roll - it gets modified by stuff like necessity (it gets harsher if you're chopping bits off to replace, rather than just getting a new leg), counseling, and the implant itself (the more advanced it is, the more likely that they've addressed certain issues with neurofeedback). If you want to play it out, take Phantom Limb as a condition (an alternative? Addicted for pain killers).<br /> <br /> When you're walking around the streets later, you can take Breaking Points for people freaking out at your cyberware. I wouldn't make that a hard mechanic - let the players determine whether or not they're bothered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T20:28:40-07:00","id":1139088,"title":"","content":"So what about say things that arent so much plug ins but complete alterations?<br /> <br /> Perhaps a complete merit/power stat chain about defining how much you are transhuman, with the top being a full body conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T00:41:05-07:00","id":1139123,"title":"","content":"I've used the alternate Attribute/Skill spreads for character creation ever since Mirrors came out. I'm a little sad that Primary/Secondary/Tertiary stuck around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T17:57:32-07:00","id":1139797,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Cyber-Psychosis</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> raises an excellent point, and one I had not considered before. Of course, this feels like the sort of thing that would open one of those thread-derailing, contentious debates.<br /> I like the suggestion that getting a new Augment is a Breaking Point, and could lead to augmentation specific conditions and tilts. revised text below. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Augmentations represent artificial modifications to a characters body that greatly enhance its capabilities, in certain cases to a superhuman degree. These augmentations typically represent cybernetic or genetic modification, but could be used to represent mystic alterations as well. The merits represent basic capabilities, how these manifest or are described is up to the storyteller and players to decide.<br /> The over-all number of dots in Augmentation merits a character can have is limited to (10 + the lower of Resolve or Stamina). <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Each time a character purchases dots a in Augmentation Merit, it is considered a Breaking Point. Failed rolls can result in specialized, Augment-related Conditions.</span> There is only so much strain the body and mind can withstand.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T10:43:26-07:00","id":1140235,"title":"","content":"Another good base for cybernetics are Demon Form Abilities. Things like Strength enhancement, radio suites, mirrored or chameleonic skin, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T01:41:15-07:00","id":1140447,"title":"","content":"The Demon Storyteller's Guide actually has a setting hack where the God-Machine has separated a city from reality into a sort of pocket reality, and the people there have cyber-augmentations that are treated like how cellphones are today. It may serve as a good baseline technology-wise.<br /> <br /> As for Infinite Macabre, it has a few...troubling aspects about it. One in particular was how the suggestions for Changelings were handled, such as making a Changeling and their Keeper into more like a typical space-opera where the Keeper was a ruler and their Changeling a lost lover...but in the conventional sense. I found it pretty squicky to read.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, thinking on how Demons and Beasts would fit into such a setting has me practically giddy. Would there be a God-Machine per star system, each as alien as the last, or are they all part of some much more gargantuan process? Could Beasts set up chambers on different planets and use that as a form of faster-than-light travel? How strange could a Demon's gadgets get and yet not be looked at as too strange by normal society - better yet, as tech advances more, could a Demon's gadgets start looking out of place by resembling older tech? Would Beasts have some kind of cosmic Dark Mother, or would they have analogues on other worlds? Could Demons or Beasts find themselves actually fitting in on spaceships for practical roles?<br /> <br /> Heck, Demons on a spaceship would have to worry about Cover as much as they would on Earth, because unlike on Earth they can't just endlessly find people to pact in new parts when their lives are picked apart. A spaceship is small, and its community smaller. A cover too worn will attract attention, and the people within may find themseles with a new, &quot;alien&quot; intruder where their doctor once was. You don't even need the God-Machine to make a Demon's life a struggle on a ship, though you may want to throw in some new kinds of threats to make it so they can't just suffice on Embeds and such...<br /> <br /> Beasts with their lairs acting as faster-than-light gateways may find themselves as covetted for travel purposes, taking Satiety as payment...or as the source of pirating goods along. A Beast's lair traits could even be used as a shortcut for expensive technology (Mirages as holograms, for example, or with said traits as security measures) or even simply being covetted as explorers who can get through scenarios without a scratch. That's to say nothing of how they may find their starbound cousins, and the nightmares they can provide...<br /> <br /> ...I really need to stop posting stuff past 1am. I get way too rambly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-18T20:46:30-07:00","id":1141644,"title":"","content":"I handled cybernetics by borrowing a Merit from the Promethean supplement Saturnine Night. Specifically, it's the Merit that lets you integrate machines into an Unfleshed. Apply them to someone or something that's organic, and you've covered the implants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T16:11:10-07:00","id":1145653,"title":"","content":"I'm a big fan of Mirrors' Extraordinary Mortals and Dark Heroes, so I wanted to finally take a stab at GibberingEloquence's suggestion of an updated list of Skill Tricks for 2E. Most are buffed, sometimes by merging 1E Skill Tricks together, in keeping with 2E's overall higher power level. A few, like Butcher, are nerfed to reflect the new scarcity of Aggravated damage. Feedback and further contributions are welcome, particularly for Mental &amp; Social Tricks; the list will be updated accordingly.<br /> <br /> Academics<br /> Computer<br /> Crafts<br /> <br /> Investigation<br /> - Always Investigating: Add Investigation to Perception, Survival, and Streetwise rolls. When Investigation applies, score exceptional success at three rather than five.<br /> Medicine<br /> - Anatomical Intimidation: Add Medicine to Intimidation rolls and to attacks against targets with recognizable anatomic features.<br /> <br /> Occult<br /> Politics<br /> Science<br /> <br /> Athletics<br /> - Fastest of Them All: Add Athletics to Speed and Initiative.<br /> - Perfect Physique: Add Athletics to Social Maneuvering rolls conducted in person.<br /> <br /> Brawl<br /> - Killer Instinct: Make All-Out Attacks and use Fighting Style maneuvers without sacrificing Defense. (Maneuvers do not stack.) <br /> - Multiple Strike: Apply attacks to all targets in reach. Subtract highest Defense. <br /> <br /> Drive<br /> - Expert Driver: Substitute Drive for Handling when higher; add Drive to car's Durability.<br /> <br /> Firearms<br /> - Trick Shot: Add higher of Intelligence or Wits to Firearms rolls when accomplishing a task (e.g. shoot out a tire) or making a targeted strike. This can eliminate penalties, but can never result in a net bonus.<br /> <br /> Larceny<br /> - Spot Concealed Weapons: Add Larceny to Investigation rolls to find concealed weapons on people or within environments; subtract Larceny from others' attempts to find concealed weapons on you.<br /> <br /> Stealth<br /> - Backstab: Subtract Stealth from opponents' Perception rolls. Add Stealth to attacks against surprised targets. Opponents' dramatic failure on Perception rolls enables you to make a Killing Blow.<br /> - Know the Shadows: Add Stealth to Perception rolls and to Investigation rolls. When Stealth applies to these rolls, score exceptional success at three rather than five.<br /> <br /> Survival<br /> - Concrete Jungle: In urban environments, add Survival to Investigation, Streetwise, and Perception rolls. When Survival applies to any of these rolls, score exceptional success at three rather than five.<br /> <br /> Weaponry<br /> - Butcher: With an edged weapon, cause an improved version of the Bleeding Tilt (Hurt Locker, pg. 143) with any successful attack. Each turn bleeding continues, mortals take 1 Aggravated damage, vampires lose 1 Vitae, and werewolves take 1 Lethal; even accelerated healing can't entirely keep up with the geyser from an open carotid. The Tilt ends with an extended Dexterity + Medicine roll (one turn/roll; [Weaponry] successes required), or with magical healing that affects Lethal damage.<br /> - Cripple: Inflict your choice of Arm Wrack or Leg Wrack on any successful attack targeting a limb; successes greater than victim's Stamina are not required.<br /> - Flashing Blades (by GibberingEloquence): 8-Again to Dodging while armed, +1 weapon damage, increase Defense by (Weaponry/2, round up)<br /> <br /> Animal Ken<br /> Empathy<br /> Expression<br /> Intimidation<br /> Persuasion<br /> Socialize<br /> Streetwise<br /> Subterfuge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-01T07:31:24-07:00","id":1145785,"title":"","content":"Addendum, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a>: would be curious to hear your thoughts on modifying Flashing Blades to add Defense vs. firearms attacks, after the fashion of Isao Machii (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qzhs1Z8Rwnk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qzhs1Z8Rwnk</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}